  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/puc900.html",
  "prefLabel": "Puc 902.23 Net Energy Metering",
  "priorExpiration": "2014-07-02",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Puc 902.23 “Net Energy Metering” means “net energy metering” as defined in RSA 362-A:1-a, III-a, namely, “measuring the difference between the electricity supplied over the electric distribution system and the electricity generated by an eligible customer-generator which is fed back into the electric distribution system over a billing period.”\n\nSource. #10502, INTERIM, eff 1-3-14, EXPIRED: 7-2-14 (from Puc 902.13)\n\nNew. #10757, eff 1-8-15 (from Puc 902.16); ss by #13080, eff 9-14-20 (formerly Puc 902.17)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/puc900.html"
